/ tbl02_columns -- columns and rows
/
/ Because a table is a dictionary of columns, t`price gives you a whole
/ COLUMN as a list. Indexing with a number gives you a ROW, which comes
/ back as a dictionary. `first t` is the first row.
/
/ The `trade` table is provided for you (see data/fixtures.q).
